The reader theme, the translation corrections and the build were produced with
the help of Claude, an AI assistant by Anthropic, under E3e's direction and
review (see "AI assistance" in README.md). This does not change the licensing
described here.

This MIT grant covers the translations and the reader theme only. It does not
extend to the documentation content described in section 1, which stays with
ImperfectLink.


3. Bundled third-party code
---------------------------

These files are generated by Sphinx and published in each language's
_static/ folder; each keeps its own licence and copyright:

  * Sphinx assets — doctools.js, searchtools.js, sphinx_highlight.js,
    documentation_options.js, language_data.js, translations.js, pygments.css,
    plus.png, minus.png, and the generated searchindex.js files.
    © the Sphinx team and contributors, BSD 2-Clause.
    https://www.sphinx-doc.org/
  * Snowball stemmers — the English, German, French and Russian stemming code
    inlined in language_data.js. © Dr Martin Porter, Richard Boulton and the
    Snowball contributors, BSD 3-Clause. https://snowballstem.org/

Full licence texts are available from the project pages listed above.


4. Trademarks
-------------

Keyboard Render Kit, Blender and the names of keyboards, keycap profiles and
manufacturers shown in the documentation belong to their respective owners and
are used here for identification only.
